Let \(B\subset\mathbb R^n\), let \(f\in C^2\) on a neighborhood of \(B\), let \(P\) be a parameter set, and let \(H:P	o\mathbb S^n\). The family \(H(P)\) is an exact parametric-Hessian model if there is a map \(p:B	o P\) such that \(
abla^2f(x)=H(p(x))\) for every \(x\in B\) and \(H(P)=\{
abla^2f(x):x\in B\}\). It is an outer parametric-Hessian model if only \[\{
abla^2f(x):x\in B\}\subseteq H(P)\] is required. In either case, repeated occurrences of the same parameter are varied jointly according to \(P\), rather than independently entry by entry.
